  "title": "Rotation-tolerant representations elucidate the time course of high-level object processing",
  "description": "This dataset contains EEG recordings from 16 participants viewing object images presented in eight different 2-D rotations, using rapid visual streams at two presentation rates (5 Hz and 20 Hz). The data support investigation of rotation-tolerant object representations and the time course of high-level visual object processing. EEG data are formatted according to the BIDS standard.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were collected from 16 participants who viewed object images shown in eight different 2-D rotations, presented in rapid visual streams at two presentation rates (5 Hz and 20 Hz).",
